{
  "meta": {
    "note": "The three intro scenes, as data rather than as pictures or as code. Each one is a moment of the game held still and animated in place: the years of the mercato waiting for a name, the two shirts with the answer landing between them, the three stars at the end of a round.",
    "why-shared": "The numbers live here for the same reason the design tokens do. Two hand-tuned copies of a scene are two different scenes within a month, and nobody would notice until the two stores were showing two different intros. iOS, Android and the desk preview all read this file; none of them owns a coordinate.",
    "frame": "The stage is the inside of the card, 398x190, origin just inside the 5 border. The card itself, its border and its shadow are drawn by the screen around the scene, not by the scene.",
    "no-words": "Nothing here is translatable. Years, a question mark, a score and shapes read the same in the three languages the app ships, which is what lets the intro carry real content instead of grey bars standing in for text."
  },

